  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 206 PM EDT Mon Jun 15 2026\n\nTo begin the period, all eyes will be on an area of interest in the \nGulf by late Wednesday into Thursday. Model guidance continues to \ndiverge on whether the system develops or not. With that said, the \npotential for tropical moisture moving over the state is increasing. \n\nPW values of two inches or greater appears possible by Thursday as a \nswath of tropical moisture moves over the region. While we are still \na few days away, it is important to understand that regardless of \nany tropical storm development, heavy rain chances continue to \nincrease across much of the state for Thursday and Friday.\n\nAs additional data become available over the next couple of days, \nplease continue to check back for the latest information. \n\nTemperatures are expect to remain near normal through much of the \nperiod given the increase in PoPs and cloud cover. Some days, \ntemperatures could even be below average.",
